# NOTE (power-law-z change): this file predates the switch of the LVK
# model's redshift evolution to a pure power law (1+z)^lam.  Its dkappa
# and zp lines are Madau-Dickinson parameters the LVK model no longer
# reads, so run_inf_lvk.py now RAISES on this file rather than sampling
# them as dead dimensions.  Kept as the record of the run it produced.
# For a new run, use lvk_gwtc5_plz.prior (or drop the dkappa/zp lines).
# Hybrid control run: LVK GWTC-5 Default 'PowerLaw + 2 Peaks' mass model
# (arXiv 2605.27226, no spins) for BOTH masses, but paired the way the
# original PISN model (intensity_models_fast.LogDNDMDQDV) pairs them --
# f(m1) f(m2) with a total-mass power law (mt/(mref(1+qref)))^beta -- instead
# of the LVK q^beta S(q m1)/Zq(m1) convention.  Run with run_inf_lvk.py and
# `pairing = mt` in the ini.
#
# Comparison logic across the three real-data control runs:
#   (1) PISN mass + mt pairing   -- realGWTC5_noevo_259ev_* runs
#   (2) LVK  mass + mt pairing   -- THIS run
#   (3) LVK  mass + q^beta       -- realGWTC5_lvk_control
# (1) vs (2) differ only in the mass model; (2) vs (3) differ only in the
# pairing function -- so the pair of comparisons disentangles mass-model
# effects from pairing-function effects.
#
# The mass priors below are deliberately IDENTICAL to lvk_gwtc5_control.prior
# (including its known imperfections vs the LVK paper), so the comparison to
# the finished control run differs only in the pairing.  The ONE substantive
# change is beta: it is now the TOTAL-MASS exponent, not the q exponent, so
# it takes the PISN real-data runs' pairing prior Normal(0, 2) (as in
# real_dat_noevo_fullsel_r.prior) instead of Uniform(-4, 7).
# Cosmology fixed to Planck; free it by replacing the first three lines with
# log_h / Omh2 / w prior lines (the model derives Om = Omh2/h^2).
h = 0.674
Om = 0.315
w = -1
# --- mass model (names mirror the popsummary release; NOTE the release's
#     lam_0 is the POWER-LAW fraction: lam_0 = 1 - f_peaks, and
#     lam_1 = f_peaks*f_p1 is the peak-1 fraction) ---
alpha_1 = Uniform(-4.0, 12.0)
alpha_2 = Uniform(-4.0, 12.0)
mbreak = Uniform(20.0, 50.0)
mpp_1 = Uniform(5.0, 15.0)
sigpp_1 = Uniform(0.1, 10.0)
mpp_2 = Uniform(25.0, 100.0)
sigpp_2 = Uniform(0.1, 10.0)
f_peaks = Uniform(0.0, 1.0)
f_p1 = Uniform(0.0, 1.0)
beta = Normal(0, 2)
# --- fixed bounds (floats -> deterministic sites; free one by swapping in a
#     distribution -- the LogQNorm axis bounds are static, so that traces) ---
mmin = 4.5
mmax = 300.0
delta_m = 4.0
# --- redshift evolution: identical to the real-data control pipeline ---
lam = TruncatedNormal(2.7, 2.0, low=-1.3, high=6.7)
dkappa = TruncatedNormal(2.9, 2.0, low=1, high=6.9)
zp = TruncatedNormal(1.9, 1, low=0, high=3.9)
zmax = 3.0
